.SH "NAME"
systemd-mute-console, systemd-mute-console@.service, systemd-mute-console.socket \- Temporarily mute kernel log output and service manager status output to the system console
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBsystemd\-mute\-console\fR\ 'u
\fBsystemd\-mute\-console\fR [OPTIONS...]
.PP
systemd\-mute\-console@\&.service
.PP
systemd\-mute\-console\&.socket
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The
\fBsystemd\-mute\-console\fR
tool and service may be used to temporarily mute the log output of the kernel as well as the status output of the service manager to the system console\&. It may be used by tools running on the console to ensure their terminal output is not interrupted by unrelated messages\&.
.PP
The tool can be invoked directly in which case it will mute the two outputs and then issue an
\fBsd_notify\fR(3)
"READY=1"
notification once that is completed\&. On
\fBSIGINT\fR
or
\fBSIGTERM\fR
output is unmuted again\&. Alternatively it can be invoked via Varlink IPC\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
The following options are understood:
.PP
\fB\-\-kernel=\fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR, \fB\-\-pid1=\fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR
.RS 4
Individually controls which output to mute\&. If true is specified the respective output is muted, if false the output is left as is\&. Defaults to true\&.
.sp
Added in version 259\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Print a short help text and exit\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print a short version string and exit\&.
.RE
